      "writtenOn": "2023-05-31T14:09:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I do like the idea of moving the color filters into a dedicated directory. We\u0027ve done that for other groups in the past (gradients, image, shaders) - color filters are actually the odd duck here, so let\u0027s do that.\n\nAlso agreed that it\u0027s a shame to undo prior work, but I don\u0027t feel real strongly about that one - there\u0027s no real intrinsic benefit to not having the headers -- other than putting everything for a single class in a single file. Of course, this kind of refactoring makes that a non-starter, so I think landing on a single h/cpp pair per-class is a principled organization.",
      "parentUuid": "0f21e97a_9adbd883",
      "revId": "15d23355d6294acc11f4dca634652f52ed41229c",
